From fbf01439676dde5dc2355998ea308fa1c7769444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:38:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] solidcore-cadir: decreasing polyline parameters, a
 rounding-only similarity check, shell members noted, normal tests

Review follow-up.
- A polyline whose parameters decrease along its samples (CADIR admits both directions) is read
  as the same map from parameter to point instead of refusing its region.
- A placement is taken as a rotation and uniform scale only to within the rounding of a matrix
  written to double precision (64 ulp), not 1e-9: diag(1, 1, 1 + 5e-10) is now refused.
- A shell's wire edges and free vertices, which a record of faces cannot hold yet, are noted on
  the region instead of left out silently.
- Tests: a negative sphere and torus (tube) radius turn the surface side and a positive one does
  not; NURBS `normal_reversed` turns it; descending polyline parameters keep their points.
- The public result fields are documented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
